Bug 2045506: Initialize the unread-count dock badge at startup on macOS even when no mail window opens. r=arschmitz,edicharry

On macOS the application keeps running with no windows open and can be relaunched (for example to apply an update) without a 3pane mail window being shown. The dock unread-count badge is driven by MailNotificationManager, whose init() is only called from the 3pane window (messenger.js loadPostAccountWizard), so in a windowless startup nothing computes or sets the badge until the user opens a window. This is why the badge disappears after an automatic update and reappears when a window is opened.

Drive MailNotificationManager.init() from MailGlue's window-independent startup path (final-ui-startup) on macOS, and guard init() so it runs only once; the later window-driven call is then a no-op.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310234


